00:32:58,760 --> 00:32:59,520
[SPEAKER_03]: Not you.

367
00:32:59,540 --> 00:33:01,461
[SPEAKER_03]: That saṅkharas are not your activities.

368
00:33:01,481 --> 00:33:02,662
[SPEAKER_03]: They're citta's activations.

369
00:33:05,654 --> 00:33:20,980
[SPEAKER_03]: So, yes, you need to learn about anatta, you need to contemplate anicca and dukkha and so on, just so to keep teaching the animal to stop regarding you as self, as I am, as, oh, look at this guy.

370
00:33:24,062 --> 00:33:30,004
[SPEAKER_03]: And, yes, it's correct, when animal is sufficiently deactivated from those activations,

371
00:33:34,747 --> 00:33:38,929
[SPEAKER_03]: It will stop regarding you as self, and then you will stop regarding it yourself, as yourself.

372
00:33:41,850 --> 00:33:44,851
[SPEAKER_03]: So, it's out of your hands then, so to speak.

373
00:33:44,891 --> 00:33:45,912
[SPEAKER_03]: Anatta is out of your hands.

374
00:33:47,212 --> 00:33:57,137
[SPEAKER_03]: You were atta, because the animal was seeing you too much of a person, basically, because of its own wilderness that you were responsible for, through not taming it.

375
00:33:58,037 --> 00:34:00,338
[SPEAKER_03]: You tamed it, became unwild,

376
00:34:02,128 --> 00:34:11,574
[SPEAKER_03]: You provided wisdom for it, the insights, the ten perceptions that the suttas talk about, which you should be providing your citta for, and it stops seeing you as a person.

377
00:34:13,515 --> 00:34:17,117
[SPEAKER_03]: And when citta stops seeing you as a person, there's nothing you can do about it yourself.

378
00:34:18,098 --> 00:34:18,938
[SPEAKER_03]: Why would you, obviously?

379
00:34:18,958 --> 00:34:21,140
[SPEAKER_03]: Because you feel relieved of the burden of personality.

380
00:34:30,105 --> 00:34:31,086
[SPEAKER_01]: So, would you say, eh...

381
00:34:32,777 --> 00:34:59,675
[SPEAKER_01]: Practically speaking, it's basically when none of the same, like you can think as much as you want, like you would say the designations, you can think as much as you want in terms of the same images, the same things that used to kind of represent you.

382
00:35:00,536 --> 00:35:00,836
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

383
00:35:01,096 --> 00:35:02,257
[SPEAKER_01]: But none of them can

384
00:35:04,092 --> 00:35:12,633
[SPEAKER_01]: Not to be... can kind of take on this extra implication, because even those extra implications can't not be seen as things.

385
00:35:12,713 --> 00:35:14,394
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, so the... exactly, exactly.

386
00:35:14,414 --> 00:35:15,634
[SPEAKER_01]: They're just seen as things.

387
00:35:15,774 --> 00:35:23,595
[SPEAKER_03]: The point is, the core of your sense of self, that you feel, is the citta's perception of you.

388
00:35:25,316 --> 00:35:26,116
[SPEAKER_03]: Let's put it that way.

389
00:35:27,616 --> 00:35:28,576
[SPEAKER_03]: You don't see a citta.

390
00:35:29,236 --> 00:35:33,177
[SPEAKER_03]: You don't see that... where that core, where that activation comes from.

391
00:35:34,070 --> 00:35:35,591
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you just bundle it all together.

392
00:35:37,171 --> 00:35:42,833
[SPEAKER_03]: You start seeing citta enough, like a prerequisite for sotāpati, that core will be undermined.

393
00:35:44,614 --> 00:35:45,354
[SPEAKER_03]: Everything else remains.

394
00:35:45,374 --> 00:35:52,097
[SPEAKER_03]: The shell of you remains, but the core is now switched off, gone, destroyed.

395
00:35:53,697 --> 00:35:55,398
[SPEAKER_03]: That's tyātavāda when it's abandoned.

396
00:35:56,058 --> 00:36:00,380
[SPEAKER_03]: Then, you might have remnants, well, you will have remnants of I am and stuff, but the same principle remains.

397
00:36:05,049 --> 00:36:32,701
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's also, see, to the extent that you are overlooking your internal body as the totality of your experience as a whole, to that extent there is a basis for that core of perception that comes from citta, seeing you as a person, for you to place it somewhere in that internal totality of your body, somewhere peripherally, at the back, neither here nor there.

398
00:36:33,649 --> 00:36:42,634
[SPEAKER_03]: That's also why, through realizing that, well, backwards, forwards, at the back of my head, front, doesn't matter, up, down, in any direction, physicality is there.

399
00:36:43,355 --> 00:36:44,456
[SPEAKER_03]: The four great elements.

400
00:36:44,596 --> 00:36:46,557
[SPEAKER_03]: Nothing cannot be part of this.

401
00:36:47,718 --> 00:37:00,986
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's how you delineate citta clearer and recognize that the activating core of that heart of I am, it's actually citta just mistakenly sees you as a person.

402
00:37:01,126 --> 00:37:01,606
[SPEAKER_03]: And when you...

403
00:37:02,237 --> 00:37:02,457
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

404
00:37:02,777 --> 00:37:11,420
[SPEAKER_03]: And when you recognize that anything the citta would be seeing, the animal would be seeing when it looks at you, is the four great elements, nothing else.

405
00:37:11,640 --> 00:37:16,481
[SPEAKER_03]: The bile, the skin, the space in between, the wind.

406
00:37:18,062 --> 00:37:19,142
[SPEAKER_03]: Then the citta will stop.

407
00:37:19,362 --> 00:37:27,905
[SPEAKER_03]: It will still see, maybe, a remnant of what it used to think was a full-blown person I am, but that whole source

408
00:37:28,917 --> 00:37:32,598
[SPEAKER_03]: Of ākhaṅkāra and mamaṅkāra, isn't it?

409
00:37:32,618 --> 00:37:36,399
[SPEAKER_03]: Eye-making and mind-making that comes from citta is going to be depleted.

410
00:37:39,440 --> 00:37:47,303
[SPEAKER_03]: While everything, like even your speech patterns and ways of expression and reference, it remains completely unchanged because that's not where the self was.

411
00:37:51,024 --> 00:37:56,606
[SPEAKER_03]: So that's also why it's relevant to pervade with the cool illuminating pleasure

412
00:37:57,765 --> 00:38:07,676
[SPEAKER_03]: of the hindrance-free citta, the entire extent of the totality of your body internally, so that the whole thing will be seen as external to citta.

413
00:38:08,957 --> 00:38:12,821
[SPEAKER_03]: No part left unilluminated, unpervaded.

414
00:38:13,962 --> 00:38:20,549
[SPEAKER_03]: Thus, no part can be assumed as a basis for that lingering senses of I am that might be remaining.

415
00:38:26,298 --> 00:38:52,616
[SPEAKER_01]: It reminded me also that what you just said now, and you said it earlier as well, but it reminded me of what you were saying in regards to ānāpānasati as well, about contrasting the internal physicality of the body with the act of breathing and the perception of breathing.

416
00:38:54,838 --> 00:39:00,980
[SPEAKER_01]: So as to, yeah, further, basically, to... Outline.

417
00:39:01,280 --> 00:39:01,940
[SPEAKER_03]: The extent of it.

418
00:39:01,960 --> 00:39:03,141
[SPEAKER_01]: The extent of both.

419
00:39:03,721 --> 00:39:04,541
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly, yeah.

420
00:39:04,581 --> 00:39:10,403
[SPEAKER_03]: By outlining the extent of the internal physicality, you're revealing what citta is not.

421
00:39:11,643 --> 00:39:12,643
[SPEAKER_03]: What citta cannot be.

422
00:39:12,683 --> 00:39:21,806
[SPEAKER_03]: That's why after you would have been doing these contrasting practices with regard to the body, then, sort of, comes to the feelings, and then the mind.

423
00:39:24,825 --> 00:39:35,729
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's not... Could you say that's basically, or it could be thought of just another type of description of jhāna?

424
00:39:35,769 --> 00:39:37,490
[SPEAKER_01]: This was one kind of question I had.

425
00:39:37,590 --> 00:39:38,991
[SPEAKER_01]: Or is it a completely different thing?

426
00:39:39,231 --> 00:39:41,132
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, of course.

427
00:39:41,212 --> 00:39:41,832
[SPEAKER_03]: It's all jhāna.

428
00:39:42,072 --> 00:39:42,432
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

429
00:39:42,592 --> 00:39:43,152
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, good.

430
00:39:43,513 --> 00:39:44,733
[SPEAKER_03]: Contemplating dead bodies.

431
00:39:45,173 --> 00:39:45,814
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

432
00:39:45,914 --> 00:39:48,635
[SPEAKER_03]: They will outline your own internal physicality as unownable.

433
00:39:48,655 --> 00:39:49,155
[SPEAKER_03]: It's jhāna.

434
00:39:49,255 --> 00:39:49,455
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

435
00:39:50,315 --> 00:39:52,096
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just different directions of approaching it.

436
00:39:52,116 --> 00:39:54,237
[SPEAKER_03]: So, that's... And I think,

437
00:39:54,710 --> 00:40:13,162
[SPEAKER_03]: I think commentaries, the traditional Theravāda, sort of, with Siddhimāga and company, kind of understood that, in a sense of, through studying the texts, they saw that, you know, the magical, mystical jhāna occurs out of all these different, seemingly different practices.

438
00:40:14,022 --> 00:40:21,987
[SPEAKER_03]: So, I remember, it was some, it was like some Theravāda manual on meditation, a long time ago, and it was like basically compiling all the

439
00:40:25,369 --> 00:40:30,158
[SPEAKER_03]: all the objects that can lead to jhāna, on the basis of the suttas.

440
00:40:31,320 --> 00:40:37,071
[SPEAKER_03]: So, it was ānāpānasati, it was contemplating corpses, it was loving-kindness,

441
00:40:37,665 --> 00:40:45,394
[SPEAKER_03]: So, it was all presented as these different methods they would magically take to jhāna, not recognizing that actually doing those things rightly is already jhāna.

442
00:40:45,494 --> 00:40:45,914
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

443
00:40:46,455 --> 00:40:48,377
[SPEAKER_03]: It's already what jhāna is.

444
00:40:48,417 --> 00:40:48,577
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

445
00:40:48,597 --> 00:40:54,183
[SPEAKER_01]: So, this is really useful for me because that was one of the big confusions I used to have when reading the suttas.

446
00:40:54,223 --> 00:40:59,229
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, because, you know, you ask him what's the right meditation and the answer is jhāna.

447
00:40:59,449 --> 00:40:59,629
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

448
00:40:59,769 --> 00:41:04,531
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, at the same time, you have, like, all of these different suttas, seemingly talking about different things.

449
00:41:04,551 --> 00:41:05,232
[SPEAKER_01]: Different things, yeah.

450
00:41:05,432 --> 00:41:07,553
[SPEAKER_01]: Nine percept, develop these nine perceptions.

451
00:41:07,593 --> 00:41:07,933
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

452
00:41:08,353 --> 00:41:10,794
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can say, well, yeah, okay, that's, like, makes sense.

453
00:41:10,834 --> 00:41:12,415
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, how does the, you know... Yeah.

454
00:41:12,435 --> 00:41:13,596
[SPEAKER_01]: Where does jhāna come in here?

455
00:41:13,616 --> 00:41:14,196
[SPEAKER_01]: Jhāna come into it?

456
00:41:15,016 --> 00:41:18,558
[SPEAKER_01]: And, yeah, it simplifies things considerably.

457
00:41:18,578 --> 00:41:19,979
[SPEAKER_03]: Jhāna is purification.

458
00:41:20,159 --> 00:41:21,339
[SPEAKER_03]: Jhāna is contemplation.

459
00:41:21,379 --> 00:41:25,761
[SPEAKER_03]: Jhāna is meditation, in the correct usage of that term.

460
00:41:26,042 --> 00:41:26,262
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

461
00:41:27,382 --> 00:41:28,943
[SPEAKER_03]: Jhāna is not concentration.

462
00:41:32,177 --> 00:41:58,373
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, like, one of the things I was kind of thinking about asking as well, in regards to this, was, yeah, we were just speaking about this, I suppose, contemplation of, or developing perception of, with this, this is, without this, this isn't, or, as you were, you would put it, like, the two points of view, thinking about that, or bearing this in mind.

463
00:41:59,755 --> 00:42:10,461
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you're doing jhāna.

464
00:42:10,521 --> 00:42:12,703
[SPEAKER_01]: That is another way of describing it.

465
00:42:13,063 --> 00:42:14,444
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's very efficient.

466
00:42:16,825 --> 00:42:17,706
[SPEAKER_03]: It goes right to the middle.

467
00:42:19,607 --> 00:42:25,910
[SPEAKER_03]: But you can see, like, even sensory strength is doing jhāna, is doing samādhi.

468
00:42:27,691 --> 00:42:28,892
[SPEAKER_03]: That's only the beginning.

469
00:42:30,450 --> 00:42:33,111
[SPEAKER_03]: Freeing yourself from that and the desert.

470
00:42:33,251 --> 00:42:40,395
[SPEAKER_03]: It's not like, again, it's not something, oh, yeah, yeah, we got to do that, but the, you know, the real meat of the practice is this method or something.

471
00:42:40,415 --> 00:42:40,675
[SPEAKER_03]: No, no.

472
00:42:40,755 --> 00:42:42,796
[SPEAKER_03]: That is already the beginning of your jhāna practice.

473
00:42:46,258 --> 00:42:52,280
[SPEAKER_03]: Not allowing images to take the center stage, not grasping the signs and features while they're pressuring you, while you're enduring them.

474
00:42:52,741 --> 00:42:53,881
[SPEAKER_03]: It's doing the jhāna practice.

475
00:42:57,783 --> 00:42:59,744
[SPEAKER_03]: Dwelling in seclusion, recognizing the extent

476
00:43:01,159 --> 00:43:12,084
[SPEAKER_03]: of the hindrances that hinder you through the movement of your wild animal, because you're wrongly attending to it, that's already jhāna practice.

477
00:43:13,805 --> 00:43:24,390
[SPEAKER_03]: Taming the wild animal, giving it rewards at the right time to recognize for itself, providing it with the ten perceptions, as that sutta says, that's already jhāna practice.

478
00:43:27,752 --> 00:43:30,733
[SPEAKER_03]: When that whole training

479
00:43:33,647 --> 00:43:55,002
[SPEAKER_03]: On the basis of prior development of virtue and the non-wrong livelihood, when that whole practice then is stable, steady, became your mode of being, as you said, you will feel debt-free, prison-free, cross the desert successfully.

480
00:43:56,483 --> 00:43:56,903
[SPEAKER_03]: And now,

481
00:43:58,305 --> 00:43:59,366
[SPEAKER_03]: Don't fall from that state.

482
00:43:59,406 --> 00:44:00,247
[SPEAKER_03]: Don't become careless.

483
00:44:00,267 --> 00:44:01,488
[SPEAKER_03]: Don't allow center images.

484
00:44:01,628 --> 00:44:04,250
[SPEAKER_03]: Don't think you did the work, because there's still work to be done.

485
00:44:06,532 --> 00:44:27,169
[SPEAKER_03]: So, then you pervade your body with that cool, illuminating pleasure of the unobstructed citta that's there, superimposed to your experience of your physicality, totality, internally as a whole, until there's no parts left that can serve as a basis for any assumption of I am and mine.

486
00:44:30,931 --> 00:44:40,895
[SPEAKER_03]: And then, when that's developed, make sure that you regard even that purified, bright, clean, free from hindrances, experience as...

487
00:44:41,575 --> 00:44:45,517
[SPEAKER_03]: But even this is a debt, is a dart, is a boil, is a burden.

488
00:44:46,937 --> 00:44:48,278
[SPEAKER_03]: Nothingness is truly better.

489
00:44:49,258 --> 00:44:51,159
[SPEAKER_03]: And then, citta will turn away even from that.

490
00:44:52,219 --> 00:44:53,320
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's when there is nothing left.

491
00:44:53,740 --> 00:44:54,580
[SPEAKER_02]: No more work to be done.

492
00:44:56,921 --> 00:44:57,922
[SPEAKER_03]: That's why this sutta say,

493
00:45:00,483 --> 00:45:05,465
[SPEAKER_03]: One can become an arahant on the basis of the first jhāna, or the second, or the third, or the fourth.

494
00:45:05,525 --> 00:45:05,806
[SPEAKER_03]: How?

495
00:45:06,366 --> 00:45:10,067
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, by fully studying his mind in the first jhāna, and then, by instructing.

496
00:45:10,127 --> 00:45:11,308
[SPEAKER_03]: Okay, now, monk, great.

497
00:45:11,508 --> 00:45:21,472
[SPEAKER_03]: That pure, blameless, factually developed mode of being that you would have cultivated, regard that now, same, as a doubt, as a debt.

498
00:45:22,853 --> 00:45:25,914
[SPEAKER_03]: And citta will want nothing to do with it.

499
00:45:25,934 --> 00:45:29,376
[SPEAKER_03]: And that means nothing will be binding you, form or formless.

500
00:45:31,715 --> 00:45:33,236
[SPEAKER_00]: Traces of being, so to speak.

501
00:45:39,458 --> 00:45:52,542
[SPEAKER_03]: So, for you, it's to provide, clarify, protect, restrain the extent, so that you can recognize it and illuminate it through your instruction, not through some mystical revelation.

502
00:45:54,503 --> 00:45:55,503
[SPEAKER_03]: You need to train it.

503
00:45:56,244 --> 00:45:58,504
[SPEAKER_03]: You need to be providing these perceptions for it.

504
00:45:59,305 --> 00:46:00,465
[SPEAKER_03]: You might not see it right away,

505
00:46:01,057 --> 00:46:07,146
[SPEAKER_03]: But if you keep it in front of it, that's your bhāvana, that's your work, the time will come when it will look and see it.

506
00:46:08,328 --> 00:46:10,431
[SPEAKER_03]: And then it will be impossible to not understand it.

507
00:46:12,273 --> 00:46:15,178
[SPEAKER_03]: So that's the whole patience aspect of practice.

